# NOTHING TOUCHES THE BYTES IN THIS REPOSITORY.
#
# Without this line, Git for Windows applies core.autocrlf=true — the factory
# default — and converts line endings on clone. A .jws with CRLF does NOT
# verify: the signature is over bytes, and changing one byte breaks it.
#
# The result would be a silent failure, on the verifier's side, for an entire
# operating system, without anyone having touched anything.
#
# It must be here from the FIRST commit: adding it later does not fix the
# people who already cloned.
* -text
